  "thumbnailAlt": "Customer Complaint form beside a photo of a smiling barista in an apron serves a customer at a cozy cafe counter",
  "content": {
    "intro": "A customer complaint form is a form that records what went wrong, when and where it happened, and what the customer wants done about it so a business can investigate fairly and respond within a set time. This template asks for the desired resolution in plain options (refund, replacement, apology, repair) so you know the customer's expectation before you pick up the phone.",
    "audience": "Retail stores, restaurants, hotels, service companies, clinics' front offices and any business that needs a written complaint log for quality or regulator reviews.",
    "useCases": [
      "A complaints link in order confirmation and receipt emails",
      "A QR code at the till or reception for in-person complaints",
      "Logging phone complaints so staff record every case the same way",
      "Building a monthly complaints register for quality reviews"
    ],
    "tips": [
      "Turn on the email copy to the respondent so the customer gets a dated record of their complaint straight away.",
      "Use the per-question charts to spot patterns, such as most complaints coming from one location or one type of issue.",
      "Edit each response to log your outcome; the edit history shows who updated the case and when, which helps if a complaint is escalated."
    ],
    "faq": [
      {
        "question": "What should a customer complaint form include?",
        "answer": "The customer's name and contact details, the order or reference number, the date and location of the problem, the type of complaint, a description of what happened, any evidence such as photos or receipts, the resolution they want and their preferred contact method."
      },
      {
        "question": "How quickly should a business respond to a complaint?",
        "answer": "Many businesses acknowledge a complaint within one or two working days and aim to resolve it within two to four weeks. Some industries have formal deadlines set by a regulator, so check the rules that apply to your sector and location."
      },
      {
        "question": "Why ask customers what resolution they expect?",
        "answer": "It tells you up front whether the customer wants a refund, a replacement, a repair or simply an apology. Knowing that makes the first reply more useful and often settles the complaint faster."
      },
      {
        "question": "Should I keep a record of complaints?",
        "answer": "Yes. A complaints log helps you spot repeat problems, train staff and show auditors or regulators how complaints were handled. Exporting responses to Excel or CSV gives you that log without retyping."
      }
    ]
  },
